cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "formants_mak: Real-Time Formants and Bandwidths for Visual Biofeedback"
abstract: >-
  A Python/Tkinter application that captures a single microphone input
  and tracks the first five vocal-tract formants (F1-F5) and their
  bandwidths in real time, plotted as a scrolling graph for visual
  biofeedback in articulation therapy, vowel-quality training and
  voice/speech analysis. Formants are estimated with Praat's Burg LPC
  method (via parselmouth), gated by a built-in YIN F0 estimator, and
  re-matched against language-specific expected formant targets
  (built-in Turkish and English presets, user-defined languages via
  JSON/Excel form) within a configurable fidelity band. formants_mak is
  the free, open-source academic module of the Sonus et Vox voice
  biofeedback suite, intended for research and teaching; the other
  modules (rtime_mak, resonance_mak, harmonicity_mak) are commercial
  applications available at https://sonusetvox.lemonsqueezy.com/
